<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muawiya I</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan, Muawiya, Muawiyah, Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muawiya I was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>, ruling from 661 to 680. As governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> he opposed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Ali in the first Muslim civil war, and after Ali's death he became caliph, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>. He moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and established hereditary succession by nominating his son Yazid.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muawiya-i.jpg" alt="Muawiya I" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploader) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arab-Sasanian_coin_of_Muawiyah_I,_struck_at_the_Fasa_mint_in_Darabjird_(Fars).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
